# HS2 (docs/ui-fit/README.md, "2j"). Every phone surface that mounts an
# error or status line on a condition, with exactly how many such lines it
# has. `pnpm check:stays-put` fails on
# any file missing here, and on any count that no longer matches, in either
# direction.
#
# One entry per line: `<sites> <path>`. A blank line ends a group, and each
# group's `#` lines must include one starting `Placement:` (why mounting it
# moves no control) or `Grandfathered:`. A new entry, or a raised count, goes
# in its own group under `Placement:`; it never joins or raises the
# grandfathered group. The usual way out is not a reason but `Reserved`
# (@some-ui/shared), which keeps the line's room and is not a site.
#
# This file is where HS2 is reviewed. The check counts; it does not judge.

# Placement: below Save, the last control, on a page that grows down; walked
# by stays-put.spec.ts (HS1).
2 packages/ui/aph/src/components/aph-log/index.tsx

# Placement: after the last control of a page that grows down: the incident
# session's lines after its screen, the record screen's after Pass, the
# session files' after the files held, Rust Rounds' after the screen (a
# card's aside after Next), Game Week's refusal after the bite's row;
# walked by stays-put-rounds.spec.ts (HS1).
1 packages/ui/game-week/src/components/game-week/index.tsx
2 packages/ui/leetype/src/components/incident/incident-session/index.tsx
